**Troy Goode wrote lib/index.js and still holds most of it: 159 of 238 lines (66.8%) if two of his addresses are one person.** The file has 62 non-merge commits from 24 addresses. Line counts come from `git blame -w -M`, as of HEAD.

**Who shaped it, oldest first**
- **Troy Goode** made the first commit on 2013-01-30 ("first commit") and added case-insensitive header lookup and the `origin: false` CORS switch the same day. He kept committing to the file until 2016-08-23, and one more commit under a second address in April 2026.
- **2013:** Damien Klinnert, Simon Mansfield (3 commits), Eric di Domenico and Mathias Buus each made small changes.
- **2014–2015:** Typicode, Alberto Leal, Shane Tomlinson and Igor Soarez each made one commit. Raymond Feng made one in 2015.
- **Later:** Douglas Christopher Wilson (4 commits) and alex94puchades (5) are the next biggest contributors. Hannah Wolfe, Eran Tiktin, LuisEGR, max.laverse and others made one commit each.

**Whose code is still there**

| Author | Lines | Share | Commits |
|---|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode (2 addresses) | 159 | 66.8% | 29 |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 22 | 9.2% | 4 |
| alex94puchades | 16 | 6.7% | 5 |
| Raymond Feng | 7 | 2.9% | 1 |
| LuisEGR | 6 | 2.5% | 1 |
| max.laverse | 6 | 2.5% | 1 |

The remaining 18 people hold 22 lines (9.2%) between them. Damien Klinnert, Typicode and four others have 0 lines left.

**Caveats**
- **Merged identity:** Troy Goode appears as `<email redacted>` and `troy@laptop.example`. Merged, that is 159 lines (66.8%) and 29 commits. Unmerged, `<email redacted>` has 147 lines (61.8%, 28 commits) and the laptop address has 12 lines (1 commit). The merge is a guess from the matching name and the addresses. I did not write a `.mailmap`, because you only asked a question.
- **Reformat commit left out:** `62628c0` ("style: reformat js with 4-space indent and double quotes", Fiona Formatter, 2026-04-12) changed 428 lines in this file, and the table above does not count it. I confirmed with `git show --stat` that it only touched whitespace and quotes across this file and three test files. If you count it, Fiona Formatter would hold 32 lines (13.4%) and Troy Goode 138 lines (58.0%).
- **Bus factor:** it is 1, measured on this file by surviving lines. Troy Goode alone holds more than 50%, and 3 authors are needed to reach 80%. Unmerged, 4 authors are needed to reach 80%.
- **No exclusions:** I saw no dropped files or bots in this output.
- **What the numbers miss:** they say nothing about quality, review or design input, or code that was deleted.

